  "definitions": {
    "public_downloadable": "Disjoint union of irexp_commercial, irexp_non_commercial, irexp_sharealike, and irexp_other. These are the redistributed JSONL files on the Hub.",
    "commercial_pool": "Every row in data/irexp_commercial.jsonl.gz. Each counted row has license_pool equal to commercial.",
    "research_corpus": "The multi-licence accounting total on the dataset card (239,735): the four public pools plus 8,895 empty/unknown-licence rows. Those 8,895 rows are not a Hub file.",
    "at_least_one_ir_band": "ir_bands_cm-1 is a list whose length is at least 1.",
    "nonempty_nmr_string": "h_nmr or c_nmr is a Python str and strip() is not empty. Null, missing, and non-strings fail. Whitespace-only strings would fail; none occurred. The rule does not require a chemical shift, so a field whose entire text is 1H, 13C, 2CO, or 3 is still counts.",
    "released_structure": "has_structure is true OR structure_tier is A, B, C, or D. Tier X is withheld. Null structure_tier is not a released structure.",
    "complete_triple": "One row with at least one IR band, a non-empty 1H string, a non-empty 13C string, and a released structure. This is the four-way conjunction the previous ICLR manuscript called a quadruple (39,118 on the 121,233-record corpus).",
    "inchikey14": "The connectivity block of inchikey: the substring before the first hyphen. On every complete-triple row the key matched ^[A-Z]{14}-[A-Z]{10}-[A-Z]$, so the block is the first 14 characters. Unique counts are the size of that set. A molecule in two licence pools is one key in the public union.",
    "tier_none": "structure_tier is null. The string none does not appear. Null is reported as none so the counts line up with the dataset card."
  },
